    "rationale": "Each of the 10 distinct 16x16 tiles (6 A, 4 B) is loaded exactly once, hitting the 2560-byte DMA lower bound. B[0,0] and B[1,0] stay resident at spad rows 16/32 for all j=0 outputs; B[0,1]/B[1,1] then replace them at 32/0 for j=1, exploiting persistence so A[2,0] and A[2,1] survive the j switch and are reused for output tile (2,1) without a reload. Each output tile is computed as K-slice 0 (overwrite, out_addr bit30=0) plus K-slice 1 (accumulate, bit30=1) into accumulator rows 0-15, then mvout with bit31/bit29 set; all preloads carry real bd addresses and every compute uses accumulated=false with bd=4294967295 as required. 45 commands total."
